*** Spoily-ish Message ***

















Price ID scrolls and then stash the ones over $200.

You can probably read the others safely.  Here's what you do:

Wear one piece of armor that you would neither mind destroying nor
enchanting.

Wield a weapon that would not be useless if enchanted nor missed if
destroyed.

Have in your inventory a spent wand or an ability ring, something that
can be charged.

Don't have any scrolls or potions on you until you know ?oFire.

I'm sure there are a few more I'm forgetting, but basically, you want
to make it safe to read an unidentified scroll, but more than this,
you don't want that scroll to be wasted, no matter what it turns out
to be.

Of course you should bless anything before you read/use it un-ID's but
for most characters that's not really a choice.  Just don't use
anything that's cursed, unless you are sure you know what you're
doing.


In my games, potions generally go unused and remain stashed for a
while, often waiting until I have *Two* unicorn horns.  Why?   Because
where some players say "dip a useless tool in case of polymorph", my
characters want to dip a unicorn horn *hoping* for poly.  See the
difference?


Ring ID can really be tough.  As the list of what things "might be"
gets shorter, then you have fewer and fewer effects to deduce.  But at
first, it's daunting, so rings and amulets are often the first things
chosen once I have ?oID.


